(D5: Discrepancy 5 - `Read from` and `Read line from` used to disagree
 about whether a dead handle is an error, and `Read from` disagreed with
 itself between a negative descriptor and a merely invalid one. A failed
 open leaves descriptor -2; `Read from` that handle was silently a 0-byte
 read while `Read line from` set the flag. Against descriptor 2147483647
 both set the flag.
 **RESOLVED - fixed by vox #48 (0.4.8), the same change that fixed D4.**
 Re-run against current main, `Read from` a failed handle now sets the flag
 too, so the two verbs agree in both directions. The buffer is still left
 at size 0 by each dead read, which is the truthful answer.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/D5.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   the failed open set the error flag
   -2
   Read from a failed handle set the error flag
   0
   Read line from a failed handle set the error flag
   0
   Read from an invalid descriptor set the error flag
   Read line from an invalid descriptor set the error flag
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
(A handle whose open failed - its descriptor is a negative errno.)
open a file for reading called missing at "vf_scratch/files/absent.txt".
On error print "the failed open set the error flag".
print missing's descriptor.
a buffer called chunk is 16 bytes in size.
Read from missing into chunk.
On error print "Read from a failed handle set the error flag".
print chunk's size.
Read line from missing into chunk.
On error print "Read line from a failed handle set the error flag".
print chunk's size.
(The same two reads against a descriptor that is merely invalid, not negative.)
open a file for reading called bogus at 2147483647.
Read from bogus into chunk.
On error print "Read from an invalid descriptor set the error flag".
Read line from bogus into chunk.
On error print "Read line from an invalid descriptor set the error flag".
